WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.648
Episode six: your first optimization.

2
00:00:02.648 --> 00:00:09.947
This video assumes APEX installed with OPM Flow, as in episode one, and a terminal in the APEX folder.

3
00:00:09.947 --> 00:00:16.226
By the end, you can run an optimization with APEX.

4
00:00:16.226 --> 00:00:21.773
The case: examples/optimization/3well/enopt.toml is PET's popt tutorial.

5
00:00:21.773 --> 00:00:36.086
Its folder holds the configuration, the deck template deck.mako and, for the robust variant, models.npz.

6
00:00:36.086 --> 00:00:38.968
Controls: the values the optimizer changes.

7
00:00:38.968 --> 00:00:55.366
Here, two control variables, each with its initial values, its bounds and a variance.

8
00:00:55.366 --> 00:01:04.053
An objective of a simulator's responses (registry response_objectives) runs each column of controls as one simulation.

9
00:01:04.053 --> 00:01:17.941
Here the objective is the net present value, NPV, as -NPV in millions: minimising it maximises NPV.

10
00:01:17.941 --> 00:01:36.803
For an objective computed by a simulator, start with enopt: it estimates the gradient from an ensemble and needs no derivatives.

11
00:01:36.803 --> 00:01:53.566
The simulators and executors are the history-matching ones (opm_flow, eclipse, process, ...): here OPM Flow, on four processes.

12
00:01:53.566 --> 00:01:59.021
Now we run it, as in the page's step one, with a few iterations first: here three.

13
00:01:59.021 --> 00:02:04.210
A successful run prints its progress and writes history.jsonl and result.json.

14
00:02:04.210 --> 00:02:20.903
We cut the wait; its real length is in the description.

15
00:02:20.903 --> 00:02:30.441
--max-iterations N stops after N accepted steps in this invocation, and the run can be resumed.

16
00:02:30.441 --> 00:02:41.686
The run directory is runs/&lt;name&gt;/ next to the configuration: here, runs, then the run's name, three-well enopt.

17
00:02:41.686 --> 00:02:59.413
Open history.jsonl to see how the objective fell, one row per accepted step.

18
00:02:59.413 --> 00:03:07.928
evaluations.jsonl in the run directory records every simulated evaluation, with its value and responses.

19
00:03:07.928 --> 00:03:14.640
Simulation folders are in simulations/eval_&lt;id&gt;/.

20
00:03:14.640 --> 00:03:28.227
So: the configuration names the controls, the objective, the optimizer and the simulator; apex optimize runs it, a few iterations at a time; and result.json holds the best controls.

21
00:03:28.227 --> 00:03:34.755
Next, episode seven compares optimizers in a study.

22
00:03:34.755 --> 00:03:40.255
Thank you for watching.
